The weave is the flow of magic through the world, felt by a caster as a current that slows, clumps and thickens from place to place. It mends itself with time, so a wound in it has to be held open to last.

The weave is the interface layer between the [[Phenomena/Aetheric Field|Aether]] below and the [[Phenomena/YuDaan's Nine-fold Treatise|Enneract]] above. A weave is naturally formed when a cumulative mass of information collects at a point on the Enneract, forcing a connection to the underlying Aetheric field. Most [[Phenomena/Locality|localities]] have the requisite mass to form a weave, and there are recorded events of individuals successfully accumulating enough to artificially generate one.

As an interface, the weave allows beings to safely draw energy from the Aether without exposing themselves to the dangerous undercurrent. The techniques used to draw from a weave are specific to that weave, so a mage from one locality will likely be unable to cast magic in another without great effort and preparation.

Drawing energy out of a person, a heart or an area damages the weave where it is done, and enough of it leaves the whole neighborhood fragile. A fragile weave lets a fracture open onto the void. The tithe asked aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] left the whole of the strider weak, not just the places where it was paid, and when [[Org/Garrick Textiles/People/Letov Obratz|Letov Obratz]] was wrung out for the first tithe the tear that opened over the dance floor came of it.
